        {
            "id": "31286396",
            "user": "Wikivisual",
            "timestamp": "13:16, 23 January 2023",
            "anon": false,
            "size": "(3,939 bytes)",
            "change": 99,
            "summary": "(Saving new step-by-step photos)",
            "is_minor": false,
            "is_expert": false,
            "status": "active",
            "contribution_type": "addition",
            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "#Select the right tool for the size of the heat shrink tubing you want to expand.<br><br> Most smaller tubing is easy to stretch with needle-nose pliers. If possible, find a pair with extended ends to accommodate longer sections of tubing.<ref>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lRua0PINTog</ref>[[Image:Expand Heat Shrink Tubing Step 1 Version 2.jpg|center]]",
                    "#To stretch larger tubing, use a combination of two pliers to expand the tubing as shown in this illustration.[[Image:Expand Heat Shrink Tubing Step 2 Version 2.jpg|center]]",
                    "#*Extremely small tubing calls for tweezers with needlepoint tips, such as LTD's Tweezerman models.[[Image:Expand Heat Shrink Tubing Step 2Bullet1 Version 2.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Insert the tweezers or pliers into the tubing as far as possible. Make sure the tool used is completely closed.[[Image:Expand Heat Shrink Tubing Step 3 Version 2.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Pull the pliers apart slowly to open up the ends. If using tweezers, use a jeweler's screwdriver to help pry the tweezers apart.[[Image:Expand Heat Shrink Tubing Step 4 Version 2.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Stretch the tubing only a little at a time to avoid tearing or puncturing it.[[Image:Expand Heat Shrink Tubing Step 5 Version 2.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Close the tweezers or pliers and rotate the tubing slightly.[[Image:Expand Heat Shrink Tubing Step 6 Version 2.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Repeat steps 2 through 5 until you have rotated the tubing enough to return to your starting point.<ref>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pP2x9eqCr6I</ref>[[Image:Expand Heat Shrink Tubing Step 7 Version 2.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Flip the tubing to so that the other end of it fits over the tweezers or pliers, and repeat the above steps.[[Image:Expand Heat Shrink Tubing Step 8 Version 2.jpg|center]]",
                    "#The tubing is now ready for use.[[Image:Expand Heat Shrink Tubing Step 9 Version 2.jpg|center]]"
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "#Select the right tool for the size of the heat shrink tubing you want to expand.<br><br> Most smaller tubing is easy to stretch with needle-nose pliers. If possible, find a pair with extended ends to accommodate longer sections of tubing.<ref>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lRua0PINTog</ref>[[Image:Expand Heat Shrink Tubing Step 1.jpg|center]]",
                    "# To stretch larger tubing, use a combination of two pliers to expand the tubing as shown in this illustration.[[Image:Expand Heat Shrink Tubing Step 2.jpg|center]]",
                    "#*Extremely small tubing calls for tweezers with needlepoint tips, such as LTD's Tweezerman models.[[Image:Expand Heat Shrink Tubing Step 2Bullet1.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Insert the tweezers or pliers into the tubing as far as possible. Make sure the tool used is completely closed.[[Image:Expand Heat Shrink Tubing Step 3.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Pull the pliers apart slowly to open up the ends. If using tweezers, use a jeweler's screwdriver to help pry the tweezers apart.[[Image:Expand Heat Shrink Tubing Step 4.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Stretch the tubing only a little at a time to avoid tearing or puncturing it.[[Image:Expand Heat Shrink Tubing Step 5.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Close the tweezers or pliers and rotate the tubing slightly.[[Image:Expand Heat Shrink Tubing Step 6.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Repeat steps 2 through 5 until you have rotated the tubing enough to return to your starting point.<ref>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pP2x9eqCr6I</ref>[[Image:Expand Heat Shrink Tubing Step 7.jpg|center]]",
                    "#Flip the tubing to so that the other end of it fits over the tweezers or pliers, and repeat the above steps.[[Image:Expand Heat Shrink Tubing Step 8.jpg|center]]",
                    "#The tubing is now ready for use.[[Image:Expand Heat Shrink Tubing Step 9.jpg|center]]"
                ]
            }
        },
