                    "#*[[Image:JLS_Retro_PC_sleeving_small.jpg|thumb|Needlenose pliers.]]Smaller and moderate sized heat shrink tubing is easy to stretch with needle-nose pliers. Most tubing sold is of this size. If possible, find a pair of needle-nose pliers with extended ends to accommodate longer sections of tubing.",
                    "#*[[Image:JLS_Retro_PC_sleeving_large.jpg|thumb|Large pliers in combination with regular pliers.]]Larger tubing will require larger pliers. Some tubing will benefit from the combination of pliers to leverage enough force to stretch thicker tubing. In this scenario, one plier's handles will expand the tubing, while the other pliers are used to pry them apart.",
                    "#*[[Image:JLS_Retro_PC_sleeving_mini.jpg|thumb|Needlepoint tweezers with a jeweler's screwdriver.]]Extremely small tubing calls for tweezers with needlepoint tips. A good example is LTD's Tweezerman models.",
                    "#'''Insert the tweezers or pliers''' into the tubing as far as possible. Make sure the tool used is completely closed.",
                    "#'''Pull the pliers apart''' slowly to open up the ends. If using tweezers, use a jeweler's screwdriver to help pry the tweezers apart.",
                    "#'''Stretch the tubing''' only a little at a time. Avoid tearing or puncturing it which could be the result of expanding it too fast or expanding it with too much pressure in one spot.",
                    "#'''Close the tweezers or pliers''' and rotate the tubing slightly."
                ]
            }
        },
